# Keep the build context small and free of secrets/runtime data.
#
# LESSON (twice burned): patterns that exclude directories by NAME — bare
# `storage` or anchored `/storage` — can match or be normalized to match at
# ANY level depending on the Docker version, and once excluded
# backend/app/storage/ broke the container at runtime
# (ModuleNotFoundError: app.storage). Only pattern shapes that CANNOT hit
# code paths are allowed here:
#   **/<name>   (no code dir is named node_modules/dist/__pycache__/.pytest_cache)
#   *.ext       (no code file ends in .db/.local)
# Runtime data dirs (storage/, out/) intentionally stay in the context: the
# container never uses them (STORAGE_ROOT points at the /data/storage volume),
# so at worst they add harmless build-context weight.
.git
.gitignore
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
*.db
.env
*.local
.DS_Store
